abstract: >-
  A foundational preprint proposing a typed mathematical audit calculus for
  claims that move between scientific descriptions. Version 1.1.0 adds
  certified normalized-scale families, logarithmic-rate and singular-set
  theorems, analytic zero-transfer and exact-decision bounds, and a
  zeta-DQPT instance. The package contains the paper, editable source, a
  two-page synopsis, ledgers, nine exact mathematical fixtures, and one
  deterministic execution receipt. Paper and human-readable
  documentation are CC BY 4.0; code, workflows, JSON Schema, and
  machine-readable fixture tooling are MIT licensed according to the repository
  license map.
